\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces TMA benchmark: (a) On-axis PSFs at $\lambda = 0.65\,\mu \mathrm {m}$: the observed misaligned PSF (Gaussian noise, $\sigma = 0.01\%$ of the ideal peak), the Nautilus starting point (median of the final 100 posterior samples), during differential evolution (DE) at generations 40, 114, 218 and 402 (A--D), and after 2000 generations (final). Intensity is relative to the aligned system's peak, so each panel's peak equals its Strehl ratio (log stretch, floor $10^{-4}$). Values are RMS wavefront error in waves, the RMS of the OPD difference from the nominal design. (b) RMS WFE of the best DE member at each generation; letters mark the PSFs in (a). (c) Best-member value of each alignment parameter at each generation (blue) and the injected truth (gray).\relax }}{42}{figure.caption.26}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.5}{\ignorespaces Residual on-axis OPD maps of the TMA: the difference between the nominal design and the system with residual misalignment $\boldsymbol {\theta }_{\mathrm {true}}-\mathbf {c}$, for the uncorrected system, the Nautilus starting point and the DE solution after 2000 generations and L-BFGS-B polishing. Piston is removed and tilt is retained, as in the quoted RMS WFE. Each panel has its own symmetric color scale in waves, with zero in gray. By variance, the final residual is 66\% tilt and 26\% defocus.\relax }}{43}{figure.caption.27}%
